<section class="howto">
  <div class="pmh">How to read this RCA</div>
  <ol class="actions"><li>Read sections 1 and 2 first: is this mine, and who is hurting?</li><li>Take section 4&#39;s phrase literally. &#34;Confirmed cause&#34; means two independent sources measured the same fault. &#34;Possibly because of X&#34; means work the &#34;What would confirm it&#34; list before escalating.</li><li>Section 5 names the sources. Several observations that all came through one controller count as one witness.</li><li>On the path, red is a measured break and dotted is inferred.</li><li>Section 7 is background and may be unrelated: do not file it as the cause.</li><li>Section 9 says who to call.</li></ol>
</section>



